# Beat: guided walk through bob/logfile against googleapis.desc,
# with the overrides from alice/app.desc already loaded.
#
# Invocation:
#   protolens --descriptor-set $PROTOTEXT_GOOGLEAPIS_SET bob/logfile \
#       --load-overrides alice/overrides \
#       --script beats/googleapis.desc
#
# Re-pin (must print nothing):
#   protolens --descriptor-set $PROTOTEXT_GOOGLEAPIS_SET bob/logfile \
#       --load-overrides alice/overrides \
#       --script beats/googleapis.desc script \
#     | grep 'error:'

title: The logfile, googleapis.desc

steps:
  - text: |
      bob/logfile — reopened against the full googleapis descriptor set.

      Good, our overrides are back. Let's see what the new corpus brings.

      👋 Press `2` to unfold.

    heat_cues: findings
    fold: ["/ 1"]
    node: /
    select_line: true
    advance_when:
      - visible: /3/4

  - text: |
      protolens now has a bright green cue for field number 7.
      ComputeRoutesResponse: that makes sense.
      The app also calls the Routes API.

      👋 Press `t`, commit ComputeRoutesResponse.

    heat_cues: findings
    fold: ["/ 2", "/3 1", "/4 1"]
    node: /3/4
    select_line: true
    advance_when:
      - type: /3/4 google.maps.routing.v2.ComputeRoutesResponse

  - text: |
      Field number 6: ComputeRoutesRequest. Symmetric.
      Pick version v2, like the response.

      👋 Press `t`, commit ComputeRoutesRequest v2.

    heat_cues: findings
    fold: ["/ 2", "/3 1", "/4 1"]
    node: /3/3
    select_line: true
    advance_when:
      - type: /3/3 google.maps.routing.v2.ComputeRoutesRequest

  - text: |
      👌 Perfect, the log file is fully typed.

      But there are still amber warnings: something is not quite right with the encoding.

      👋 Unfold the compute_routes_request for a closer look 🔍.

    heat_cues: findings
    fold: ["/ 2", "/3 1", "/4 1"]
    node: /3/3
    select_line: true
    advance_when:
      - visible: /3/3/3

  - text: |
      There it is: the travel_mode field has an amber diamond and is flagged ohb:
      OverHangingBytes. This indicates a non-canonical encoding:
      the DRIVE value (1) is encoded with too many bytes.

      👋 Press `w` for wire-level detail.

    heat_cues: findings
    fold: ["/ 2", "/3 1", "/3/3 1", "/4 1"]
    node: /3/3/3
    select_line: true
    advance_when:
      - wire: /3/3/3

  - text: |
      Five bytes at wire-level, where a single byte, 0x01, would be canonical.

      That's weird...

      👋 Press `w` to close the wire-level view.

    heat_cues: findings
    fold: ["/ 2", "/3 1", "/3/3 1", "/4 1"]
    node: /3/3/3
    wire_line: /3/3/3
    select_line: true
    advance_when:
      - not:
        - wire: /3/3/3

  - text: |
      There is also an amber triangle on the search_text_request field.

      👋 Unfold the search_text_request field.

    heat_cues: findings
    fold: ["/ 2", "/3 1", "/3/3 1", "/4 1"]
    node: /3/3/3
    select_line: true
    advance_when:
      - visible: /1/3/1

  - text: |
      OK, this is the same repeated_singular that we saw earlier with the network capture.
      Look: the shadowed text_query field has a bright green cue.
      protolens believes it is a google.rpc.Status, not a mere string.

      👋 Press Enter to commit the proposed google.rpc.Status override.

    heat_cues: findings
    fold: ["/ 2", "/1/1 Z"]
    node: /1/3/1
    select_line: true
    command: override /1/3/1 --as google.rpc.Status --cardinality optional --field-name status
    advance_when:
      - type: /1/3/1 google.rpc.Status

  - text: |
      Indeed, this is a good match.
      And the shadowed field even seems to contain a Google API key 🚨.

      That's bad 😠.

      👋 Press space to step.

    heat_cues: findings
    fold: ["/ 2", "/1/3 Z"]
    node: /1/3/1
    select_node: true
    search: 'value: ".*"'

  - text: |
      OK. We should report our findings.

      Let's export our annotated log file as prototext
      so that we can share it with Bob.

      👋 Navigate to the root node, press `x` (eXport), `p` (Prototext)
         and export as alice/logfile

    heat_cues: findings
    fold: ["/ 2", "/1/3 Z"]
    node: /1/3/1
    select_node: true
    search: 'value: ".*"'
    advance_when:
      - file_exists: alice/logfile

  - text: |
      Done!

      👋 Press Enter to quit.

    heat_cues: findings
    fold: ["/ 2", "/1/1 Z"]
    node: /
    command: quit
